<header id="top" class="hero"><div class="hero-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow"><i class="fas fa-sparkles"></i> Examination integrity operations</div><h1>Turn every incident into a <span>clear, accountable</span> decision.</h1><p class="hero-copy">BUK EIMS gives Bayero University Kano a calm, connected workspace for reporting, triage, case management, hearings, appeals, and institutional insight.</p><div class="hero-actions"><button id="hero-login" class="hero-button white"><i class="fas fa-arrow-right-to-bracket"></i> Enter staff workspace</button><a class="outline-button" href="#features" data-scroll="#features"><i class="fas fa-compass"></i> Explore the system</a></div><div class="hero-meta"><div class="meta-item"><i class="fas fa-circle-check"></i> Guided reporting</div><div class="meta-item"><i class="fas fa-timeline"></i> Case timelines</div><div class="meta-item"><i class="fas fa-chart-line"></i> Live insight</div></div></div><div class="hero-panel"><div class="panel-top"><span class="panel-label">BUK integrity workspace</span><span class="live-dot">Ready for staff</span></div><div class="mini-screen"><div class="mini-head"><strong>Good morning, team</strong><div class="mini-avatar">BUK</div></div><div class="mini-cards"><div class="mini-card"><strong>24</strong><small>Open cases</small></div><div class="mini-card"><strong>08</strong><small>Hearings</small></div><div class="mini-card"><strong>96%</strong><small>Tracked</small></div></div><div class="mini-list"><div class="mini-row"><div class="mini-icon"><i class="fas fa-file-circle-exclamation"></i></div><div><strong>New incident report</strong><small>Awaiting examination officer review</small></div><span class="pill">Review</span></div><div class="mini-row"><div class="mini-icon"><i class="fas fa-calendar-days"></i></div><div><strong>Committee hearing</strong><small>Today · 10:00 AM · Senate Chamber</small></div><span class="pill" style="background:#e8f7ef;color:#167243">Ready</span></div><div class="mini-row"><div class="mini-icon"><i class="fas fa-clipboard-check"></i></div><div><strong>Decision record</strong><small>Timeline and evidence are complete</small></div><span class="pill" style="background:#eaf4fa;color:#0b5c8e">Filed</span></div></div></div></div></div></header>
<div class="trust-strip"><div class="trust-inner"><div class="trust-copy">A focused digital layer for examination administration</div><div class="trust-points"><div class="trust-point"><i class="fas fa-shield-halved"></i> Controlled access</div><div class="trust-point"><i class="fas fa-clock-rotate-left"></i> Traceable history</div><div class="trust-point"><i class="fas fa-people-group"></i> Role-aware workspaces</div></div></div></div>
<section id="features" class="section"><div class="section-inner"><div class="section-kicker">One connected operating picture</div><h2>Designed around the work your teams actually do.</h2><p class="section-lead">From the first report in an examination hall to the final committee decision, BUK EIMS keeps the next action visible and the record easy to understand.</p><div class="feature-grid"><article class="feature-card"><div class="feature-icon"><i class="fas fa-file-signature"></i></div><h3>Report with confidence</h3><p>Use a guided incident wizard with student, examination, venue, offence, narrative, and optional evidence fields.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><div class="feature-icon"><i class="fas fa-inbox"></i></div><h3>Work the queue</h3><p>Examination officers can triage incoming reports, return clarifications, open cases, assign work, and keep momentum.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><div class="feature-icon"><i class="fas fa-folder-open"></i></div><h3>See the whole case</h3><p>Case timelines bring notes, hearings, appeals, decisions, and printable summaries into a single workspace.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><div class="feature-icon"><i class="fas fa-calendar-check"></i></div><h3>Coordinate hearings</h3><p>Keep hearing dates, venues, committee activity, and upcoming actions visible to the people involved.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><div class="feature-icon"><i class="fas fa-chart-column"></i></div><h3>Understand the pattern</h3><p>Use live summaries, analytics, and CSV reporting to support examination-office reviews and institutional meetings.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><div class="feature-icon"><i class="fas fa-file-pen"></i></div><h3>Never lose progress</h3><p>Save incomplete incident reports as named drafts, continue them later, and keep the reporting experience practical.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section id="workflow" class="section workflow"><div class="section-inner workflow-grid"><div><div class="section-kicker">A clear path from report to resolution</div><h2>Every action has a place.</h2><p class="section-lead">A role-aware flow gives invigilators, examination officers, HODs, deans, and committee members the right view at the right time.</p><div class="steps"><div class="step"><div class="step-number">01</div><div><h3>Capture the facts</h3><p>Record what happened while the context is fresh, with the examination and student details needed for review.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="step-number">02</div><div><h3>Triage and assign</h3><p>Review incoming reports, clarify incomplete records, open formal cases, and send tasks to the right people.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="step-number">03</div><div><h3>Hear, decide, and close</h3><p>Coordinate hearings, maintain the case timeline, process appeals, and produce a clear official summary.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="workflow-board"><div class="board-top"><span></span><span></span><span></span><div class="board-title">buk-eims / operations-console</div></div><div class="board-body"><div class="board-header"><strong>Operations overview</strong><span class="board-badge">Live workspace</span></div><div class="board-stats"><div class="board-stat"><strong>12</strong><small>Needs review</small></div><div class="board-stat"><strong>07</strong><small>Active cases</small></div><div class="board-stat"><strong>04</strong><small>Hearings</small></div></div><div class="board-lines"><div class="board-line"><i class="fas fa-inbox"></i><div><strong>Triage queue</strong><small>Review newly submitted reports</small></div><span class="pill">12</span></div><div class="board-line"><i class="fas fa-user-check"></i><div><strong>Committee assignment</strong><small>Balance case ownership</small></div><span class="pill" style="background:#eaf4fa;color:#0b5c8e">Open</span></div><div class="board-line"><i class="fas fa-file-export"></i><div><strong>Institution report</strong><small>Export current case outcomes</small></div><span class="pill" style="background:#e8f7ef;color:#167243">Ready</span></div></div></div></div></div></section>
<section id="institutional" class="section"><div class="section-inner"><div class="section-kicker">Built for institutional clarity</div><h2>A better experience for every role in the process.</h2><p class="section-lead">The interface is intentionally calm and structured: fewer dead ends, clearer ownership, and a shared language for examination incident management.</p><div class="feature-grid"><article class="feature-card"><div class="feature-icon"><i class="fas fa-person-chalkboard"></i></div><h3>For invigilators</h3><p>Report quickly, save drafts, and submit complete facts without navigating an administrative maze.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><div class="feature-icon"><i class="fas fa-briefcase"></i></div><h3>For examination officers</h3><p>Prioritize triage, assignments, hearings, communications, and operational reporting from one place.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><div class="feature-icon"><i class="fas fa-scale-balanced"></i></div><h3>For committees</h3><p>Review the timeline, evidence context, hearings, notes, and appeals before recording a decision.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="cta"><div class="cta-inner"><div class="eyebrow" style="justify-content:center"><i class="fas fa-building-columns"></i> BUK examination administration</div><h2>Make the next action obvious.</h2><p>Enter the staff workspace to review assigned work, report an incident, coordinate a hearing, or understand the current institutional picture.</p><button id="cta-login" class="hero-button white"><i class="fas fa-arrow-right-to-bracket"></i> Open staff workspace</button></div></section>
